---
title: "Theming: Customising Selections"
description: "$framework Data Grid row and cell selection styling: customise the appearance of selected rows and cells."
---

Control how selected rows and cells appear.

## Row Selections

When [row selection](./row-selection/) is enabled, you can set the colour of selected rows using the `selectedRowBackgroundColor` parameter. If your grid uses alternating row colours we recommend setting this to a semi-transparent colour so that the alternating row colours are visible below it.

```js
const myTheme = themeQuartz.withParams({
    // bright green, 10% opacity
    selectedRowBackgroundColor: 'rgba(0, 255, 0, 0.1)',

    // alternating row colours will be visible through the semi-transparent
    // selection background colour
    oddRowBackgroundColor: '#8881',
});
```

You can apply other styles to selected rows [using CSS](./theming-css/) by targeting the `.ag-row-selected` CSS class:

```css
.ag-row-selected {
    font-style: italic;
}
```

{% gridExampleRunner title="Custom Row Selection Colour" name="custom-row-selection-color"  exampleHeight=450 /%}

### High Contrast Colours on Selected Rows

If your grid uses dark text, and you set `selectedRowBackgroundColor` to a dark colour, you will find that the text is no longer visible. The grid provides `selectedRow` prefixed variants of several theme parameters to enable high contrast designs:

- `selectedRowTextColor` - the text and icon colour in selected rows.
- Every [checkbox colour parameter](./theming-widgets/#styling-checkboxes), e.g. `selectedRowCheckboxCheckedBackgroundColor`
- `selectedRowRangeSelectionBorderColor` - the border around the focused cell and [cell selections](#cell-selections)
- `selectedRowDragHandleColor` and `selectedRowDragIndicatorColor` - used in [row dragging](./row-dragging/)
- `selectedRowNoteIndicatorColor` - the indicator on cells with [notes](./notes/)
- `selectedRowValueChangeDeltaUpColor` and `selectedRowValueChangeDeltaDownColor` - value changes shown by [animate show changed cells](./change-cell-renderers/#animate-show-changed-cells)

This example uses these parameters to invert selected row colours:

{% gridExampleRunner title="High Contrast Colours on Selected Rows" name="selected-row-high-contrast"  exampleHeight=450 /%}

## Cell Selections

[Cell selections](./cell-selection/) can be created by clicking and dragging on the grid. Copying from a selection will briefly highlight the range of cells ({% kbd "^ Ctrl" /%}+{% kbd "C" /%}). There are several parameters to control the selection and highlight style:

```js
const myTheme = themeQuartz.withParams({
    // colour and style of border around selection
    rangeSelectionBorderColor: 'rgb(193, 0, 97)',
    rangeSelectionBorderStyle: 'dashed',
    // background colour of selection - you can use a semi-transparent colour
    // and it wil overlay on top of the existing cells
    rangeSelectionBackgroundColor: 'rgb(255, 0, 128, 0.1)',
    // colour used to indicate that data has been copied from the cell range
    rangeSelectionHighlightColor: 'rgb(60, 188, 0, 0.3)',

    // alternating row colours will be visible through the semi-transparent
    // selection background colour
    oddRowBackgroundColor: '#8881',
});
```

{% gridExampleRunner title="Custom Range Selection Style" name="custom-range-selection-style" /%}

### Cell Selection for Integrated Charts

When using [integrated charts](./integrated-charts/) with cell selections, the grid uses different colors to indicate the purpose of the cell ranges:

- `rangeSelectionChartBackgroundColor` - background color for cells used as chart data
- `rangeSelectionChartCategoryBackgroundColor` - background color for cells used as categories / axis labels
